# Security Rules

- Never expose secrets or commit `.env` files.
- Never hardcode API keys or credentials.
- Never weaken authentication or authorization.
- Never disable security checks to make tests pass.
- Never bypass input validation.
- Never log credentials, tokens, or sensitive customer/invoice data.
- Never introduce unsafe dynamic code execution (eval, Function constructor).
- Security-sensitive changes require explicit human review.
